# Figma Design System Rules

This document defines how to translate Figma designs into code for **Electric Maybe Shopify themes** (Liquid templates, Tailwind CSS v4, native JavaScript web components). Figma MCP output is typically React + Tailwind; treat that as design reference only and implement using this theme’s stack and conventions.

**Color work:** read `theme-color-modes.mdc` first. Climaybe matches Figma using **this theme’s existing `_styles/`** — it does not scaffold `_styles` from Figma and does not ship any theme’s collection catalog as SSOT. Discover names, then: optional brand on `<html>` (only if a brand class exists), section tone on the **section root**, children use semantic roles this theme defines, components → **atoms**. Never emit arbitrary hex or Brand ramps as Liquid classes.

---

## 1. Design System Structure

### 1.1 Discover tokens from this theme

**Discover from this repo — do not assume another theme’s Figma catalog**

Grep `_styles/` and `theme.liquid` before coding. Typical layout (paths and names vary):

- **Primitives / brand scales:** `_styles/01_theme/` — raw ramps, fonts, radii. CSS-only; never as Liquid Tailwind classes.
- **Sizes:** `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` — spacing, `max-w-*`, breakpoints. Figma `02.01` may **override stock Tailwind**; do not assume stock `max-w-*` / spacing. Grep `@theme` first.
- **Semantic colors + modes:** `_styles/02_base/` color files — background / text / border roles and `@utility` mode classes (often `color-schema-*`). Tone list = intersection of Figma modes and utilities **this theme ships**. Some themes ship `color-schema-accent-1|2|3` — that is one valid discovered pattern, not “older only.”
- **Typography:** `_styles/02_base/` type files — font and type utilities this theme defines.
- **Component tokens:** when `03.01` / `03.02` (or equivalent) exist, they map to **atoms** (`a--button`, inputs), not invented `button/height` utilities.

Do **not** enumerate or copy a Figma variable dump. Do **not** scaffold `_styles` from Figma. Map Figma color styles to this theme’s **existing** mode + semantic utilities.

**Axes are optional**

1. **Brand-on-`<html>`** — only if Brand modes and a brand class exist in `_styles/` / `theme.liquid`. One class rebinds Brand CSS variables for the tree. Not a section class. Skip when the theme has no brand class.
2. **Section tone** — mode class on the **section root**. Children stay semantic.

**Semantic roles** = what `_styles` defines under the active schema. Never hex. Never invent a missing role. Never use Brand ramps as Liquid classes. If Figma names a role this theme does not ship, use the closest existing semantic utility.

**Overridden utilities:** do not assume stock Tailwind for `max-w-*` or other roles listed in `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` (`px`, `py`, `gap`, `height`, `icon`, `text-size`). Grep first. Map Figma `lg` | `md` | `default` → `lg:` | `md:` | base **only when CSS remaps exist**.

**Components → atoms:** Use `{% render 'a--button', ... %}` (and input atoms) with size/variant params this theme documents. Do not invent `button/height` utilities. If no atom matches, compose from shipped semantic utilities — do not hex.

**Rules**

- IMPORTANT: Never hardcode hex/hsl in Liquid or CSS (`text-[#d1d1d1]`, raw `#fff`). Use semantic utilities under the active color mode (`theme-color-modes.mdc`).
- Spacing: grep `_styles/` — `02.01` / `*sizes*` may override stock Tailwind. Never arbitrary `px`.
- Typography must use this theme’s font utilities confirmed in `_styles/`.

### 1.2 Component Library

**Where components live**

- **Sections (full-width, schema-driven):** `sections/*.liquid` — e.g. `sections/s--hero-banner.liquid`, `sections/s--featured-collection.liquid`.
- **Snippets (reusable UI):**  
  - Atoms: `snippets/a--*.liquid` (e.g. `a--icon.liquid`, `a--button.liquid`, `a--input.liquid`).  
  - Molecules: `snippets/m--*.liquid` (e.g. `m--product-card.liquid`, `m--accordion.liquid`, `m--modal.liquid`).  
  - Feature-specific: `snippets/product--*.liquid`, `snippets/cart--*.liquid`, `snippets/header--*.liquid`, etc.
- **Web components (JS):** `_scripts/*.js` — e.g. `electric-modal.js`, `electric-slider.js`, `electric-disclosure.js`. Reference implementation: `_scripts/electric-modal.js`.

**Architecture**

- No React/Vue. UI is Liquid (sections + snippets) plus native JS web components.
- New UI from Figma: prefer adding or composing existing snippets/sections; add new snippets/sections only when no fit exists.
- Sections must have a valid `{% schema %}` and semantic HTML; snippets must have LiquidDoc `{%- doc -%}` and follow `.config/ai/rules/snippets.mdc` and `.config/ai/rules/liquid.mdc`.

### 1.3 Frameworks & Libraries

- **Templating:** Liquid only (Shopify theme).
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4. Entry: `_styles/main.css` (imports Tailwind, tokens, component CSS). Compiled output: `assets/style.css`.
- **Script:** Native JS only (no React/Vue). Web components with `#` private fields, AbortController for listeners, JSDoc; see `.config/ai/rules/javascript-standards.mdc`.
- **Build:** Tailwind processes `_styles/main.css`; content sources (for class scanning) are listed in `_styles/main.css` (`@source` for layout, blocks, sections, snippets, templates, assets).

### 1.4 Asset Management

- **Theme assets:** `assets/` — CSS, JS, and static files. Reference in Liquid with `{{ 'filename.css' | asset_url }}` or `{{ 'filename.js' | asset_url }}`.
- **Images:** Use Shopify CDN via filters: `{{ image | image_url: width: N }}` for responsive widths; use `srcset` where appropriate (see existing snippets/sections).
- **Icons:** Do not add new icon packages. Use the icon system below (inline SVG via `a--icon` or assets from Figma MCP when provided).
- **Figma MCP assets:** If the Figma MCP server returns a localhost (or other) URL for an image/SVG, use that source directly. Do not replace with placeholders when a real URL is given.
- Store any downloaded assets from Figma in `assets/` and reference via `asset_url`.

### 1.5 Icon System

- **Definition:** Icons are inline SVGs in `snippets/a--icon.liquid`, selected by name via `icon: 'name'`.
- **Usage:** `{% render 'a--icon', icon: 'search', size: 'base', class: '...' %}`. Parameters: `icon` (required), `class`, `color`, `size` (xxs|xs|sm|base|lg|xl), `width`/`height`, `stroke`, `animate`, `aria_label`, `aria_hidden`, etc. See LiquidDoc in `a--icon.liquid`.
- **Naming:** kebab-case (e.g. `chevron-d`, `arrow-r-up`, `circle-arrow-r`). Add new icons in the same file as new `when 'name'` branches; keep `fill="none"` and use `{{ color }}` or `currentColor` for strokes/fills.
- **Sizing:** Prefer `size` (uses `--height-icon-*` tokens); or `width`/`height` for explicit dimensions. Stroke from size or `stroke` param (`stroke-sm`, `stroke-base`, etc.).

### 1.6 Styling Approach

- **Methodology:** Utility-first with Tailwind. Custom utilities and theme in `_styles/main.css` and `_styles/02_base/*.css`, `_styles/01_theme/*.css`.
- **CRITICAL — Static classes only:** Tailwind scans at build time; Liquid runs on the server. Do not build class names with Liquid variables (e.g. no `duration-{{ x }}`, `text-{{ color }}`). Use fixed classes or conditionals that output full class names, e.g. `{% if size == 'sm' %}text-sm{% else %}text-base{% endif %}`.
- **Responsive:** Mobile-first. Use `md:` and `lg:` prefixes. Map Figma `lg` | `md` | `default` to `lg:` | `md:` | base **only when this theme’s CSS remaps exist** — not hard `px`. **Do not assume stock Tailwind** for `max-w-*` (or px/py/gap/height/icon/text-size) if `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` redefines them. Component density maps to atom params when atoms exist, not one-off utilities.
- **Semantic tokens in Tailwind:** Optional brand class on `<html>` (only if this theme ships one), section tone on the section root, children use only semantic roles from `_styles/`. Do not invent tokens, paste Figma hex, or use Brand ramps as classes. See `theme-color-modes.mdc`.
- **Custom component CSS:** Add in `_styles/` (e.g. `_styles/atoms/`, `_styles/molecules/`) and import from `_styles/main.css`.

### 1.7 Project Structure

```
_layout/theme.liquid     # Main layout
_scripts/                # Web components and utilities (native JS)
_styles/                 # Tailwind entry, tokens, component CSS
  main.css
  01_theme/              # primitives / brand scales (paths vary)
  02_base/               # sizes, semantic colors, typography (paths vary)
  atoms/, molecules/, core/
assets/                  # Compiled CSS/JS and static assets
sections/                # Liquid section files
snippets/                # Reusable Liquid snippets (a--*, m--*, etc.)
templates/               # Page templates
locales/                 # Translation files
config/                  # Theme settings
```

- **Feature organization:** Sections and snippets are named by feature or type (e.g. `product--main`, `cart--drawer`, `s--hero-banner`, `m--product-card`). Follow existing naming (prefix + `--` + descriptor).

